		"DISPLAY: Color display",
		"PARAMETER KNOBS: Knob 1, Knob 2, Knob 3, Knob 4, Knob 5, Knob 6, Knob 7, Knob 8",
		"BROWSER / MODES: Browser, Plug-in, DAW, Settings / MIDI, Play assist, Page left, Page right, Previous, Next, 4-D encoder",
		"PERFORMANCE: Fixed velocity, Octave -, Octave +",
		"WHEELS / STRIP: Pitch, Modulation, Touch strip"
	],
	"notice": "For spoken feedback, install and enable NI Accessibility Helper, Hardware Connection Service, compatible keyboard firmware and supported NI software. Run the Helper once to grant its required permissions. Accessibility is software-assisted and is not supplied by this catalogue or by a generic Web MIDI connection. Choose the performance MIDI port for notes and configure DAW integration separately. Wheel, pedal and strip assignments are editable; CC11 below is the documented default strip assignment. Polyphonic aftertouch is a hardware capability, not a mapping implemented here. Virtual keys show a chromatic reference range; octave, split and Play Assist settings can change outgoing notes. Select the profile manually if the host does not identify it: no unverified port aliases are supplied. Diagrams are original simplified schematics, not scale drawings. Physical controls without a binding are informational; use MIDI learn for configurable assignments.",
